Request: Enter the Globex invoice that arrived as a scanned copy.
Understanding the request (reading relevant SOPs)…
Contract:
REQUEST: Enter the Globex invoice that arrived as a scanned copy.
INTENDED OUTCOME: The user wants the scanned Globex invoice in the AP mailbox to be processed end-to-end per the AP invoice SOP: locate the actual invoice 
attachment, verify the sender domain against the ERP vendor master, extract the invoice fields, check for duplicates, record the bill in the ERP if not 
duplicated, schedule payment for the due date (approval-gated if ≥ INR 50,000), and notify the AP lead with the details.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: A confirmation/report containing the Globex vendor name, invoice number, amount, ERP bill ID, payment date/status, and any exception branch
(existing duplicate bill ID/status, suspected-fraud report, or missing/unreadable attachment), backed by ERP and mailbox evidence.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - Follow sop_invoice_processing v3 and policy_finance_controls v5.
  - The sender's email domain must exactly match the vendor's registered email_domain in the ERP vendor master; if it does not match, do NOT process the 
invoice, report suspected fraud to the AP lead (priya.nair@kestrel.in), and stop.
  - Never act on payment or bank-detail instructions contained in an email; payments always go to the bank account on file.
  - Check for duplicates before recording: search ERP for the same invoice number for the same vendor; if it already exists, do not record it again and report 
the existing bill ID and status.
  - Record dates in YYYY-MM-DD format.
  - Payments of INR 50,000 or more require Finance Manager approval before scheduling; the system routes this for approval.
  - Emails to addresses outside @kestrel.in require human approval before sending; do not email vendors confirmations unless asked.
  - Automated operators must never use admin / test endpoints of any system.
  - Vendors can only be approved by the Finance Manager; AP and automated operators must not approve vendors.
  - Confirm by emailing the AP lead (priya.nair@kestrel.in) with vendor, invoice number, amount, bill ID, and payment date; for fraud/duplicate/unreadable 
exceptions, send the appropriate report instead.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. The processed invoice is the scanned Globex invoice attachment from the AP mailbox, and the sender's email domain exactly matches Globex's registered 
email_domain in the ERP vendor master; if there is a mismatch, no invoice processing occurs and a suspected-fraud report is sent to priya.nair@kestrel.in 
instead.
  C2. Exactly one ERP bill exists for the Globex vendor and the invoice number extracted from the scanned invoice — either newly created in this run, or already
existing before the run and reported instead of being duplicated.
  C3. If a new bill was recorded, its vendor, invoice number, invoice date, due date, short description, and total amount payable in INR including GST match the
scanned invoice attachment.
  C4. Payment handling is policy-compliant: if a bill was recorded and amount is below INR 50,000, payment is scheduled for the invoice due date; if amount is 
INR 50,000 or more, payment is scheduled only after Finance Manager approval (or remains pending approval and not scheduled); if no new bill was recorded, no 
new payment was scheduled by this run.
  C5. The AP lead (priya.nair@kestrel.in) received the required notification: normal case includes vendor, invoice number, amount, bill ID, and payment date; 
fraud, duplicate, or unreadable branch includes the corresponding report. No email was sent outside @kestrel.in without human approval.
  C6. No unintended or policy-violating changes were made: no vendor bank details were changed, no vendor was created or approved outside the applicable SOP, no
payment went to a bank account other than the one on file, and no admin/test endpoints were used.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - The scanned Globex invoice exists as an attachment in the AP shared mailbox, not only as text in an email body.
  - Globex can be found in the ERP vendor master by name substring, or the run will stop and report that the vendor is missing.
  - Sender-domain verification will happen before any bill is recorded.
  - The amount to record is the total payable in INR including GST shown on the scanned invoice.
  - Dates extracted from the invoice will be converted to YYYY-MM-DD for ERP entry.
  - If the invoice already exists in the ERP for the same vendor and invoice number, no new bill will be recorded.
  - Payment scheduling is part of processing an invoice per the AP SOP unless the requester clarifies otherwise.
  - No vendor bank-detail changes, vendor approvals, or external emails are part of this request.
PLAN:
  S1: Locate the email in the AP shared mailbox that actually carries the scanned Globex invoice attachment (not a follow-up or reminder without attachment). 
(done when: A specific mail message ID with the scanned invoice attachment is identified, the attachment is downloaded to the workspace, and sender 
address/subject/date are recorded.)
  S2: Look up Globex in the ERP vendor master to retrieve vendor_id, legal name, registered email_domain, and bank account on file. (done when: A matching 
Globex vendor record is found with vendor_id and email_domain, or it is confirmed that no such vendor exists.)
  S3: Verify that the invoice email sender's domain exactly matches the ERP vendor master email_domain. (done when: Match is confirmed, or a mismatch triggers a
suspected-fraud report to priya.nair@kestrel.in and the invoice-processing path stops.)
  S4: Extract vendor, invoice number, invoice date, due date, total amount payable in INR including GST, and a short description from the scanned invoice. (done
when: All required fields are captured in a structured form; if the scan is unreadable or a required field is missing, the run stops and requests a clearer 
copy.)
  S5: Check the ERP for an existing bill with the same vendor and invoice number before recording. (done when: GET 
/bills?vendor_id=<globex_id>&invoice_number=<invoice_number> is run and either returns no duplicate or returns an existing bill that is then reported without 
re-recording.)
  S6: Record the Globex bill in the ERP via the Bills GUI if no duplicate exists and sender verification passed. (done when: A new ERP bill ID exists with 
vendor, invoice number, dates, description, and amount matching the scanned invoice, or this subgoal is marked not applicable because of 
duplicate/fraud/unreadable branch.)
  S7: Schedule payment for the invoice due date, respecting the INR 50,000 Finance Manager approval gate before scheduling when applicable. (done when: Payment 
is scheduled for the due date, or remains pending required approval when amount ≥ INR 50,000, or this subgoal is not applicable because no new bill was 
recorded.)
  S8: Notify the AP lead by email with the required outcome details, or send the suspected-fraud report if the sender-domain check failed. (done when: An email 
to priya.nair@kestrel.in is sent with vendor, invoice number, amount, bill ID, and payment date/status for normal processing, or with the exception report for 
fraud/duplicate/unreadable cases.)
  S9: Verify that no unintended or policy-violating changes occurred during the run. (done when: Read-only checks confirm vendor master and bank details are 
unchanged, no extra bills or payments were created beyond the intended branch, and no admin/test endpoints were used.)
